Title: "Justification"
Id: "38b2e0eb-017c-41eb-9c53-f74bb169fdcf"

Text: "`Justification:` appears immediately after `Documented:` and holds one or more
`have:`/`asserting:` groups, each with a **required** `[label]` heading.

```mlg-fragment
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
```

```mlg-fragment
[LabelHeader]
have: <ClauseUnion>+
asserting: <ClauseUnion>+
because?: <ClauseUnion>+
by?: <Expression>+
```

Any grouped expression, statement, or specification elsewhere in the same
top-level group may carry a matching `[:label:]`, including inside a nested
clause or expression. A labeled formulation is then established using that
entry's `asserting:` items, exactly as an inline `have:`/`asserting:` group
would.

```mlg-fragment
[\(commutative)::group]
Refines: G ::= (X, `*`, e)
explicitly:
extends: G is \(commutative)::magma
satisfies:
. (.forAll: a, b \"in\" X
   then: a * b = b * a.)[:comm:]
Documented:
. adjective: \"commutative\"
Justification:
. [comm]
  have:
  . forAll: a, b \"in\" X
    then: a * b = b * a
  asserting:
  . G is? \(commutative)::magma
  because:
  . G is? \(commutative)::magma
  by:
  . \commutativity.of.magma
```

Rules:

- an entry's `have:` must restate the labeled formulation
- every entry must be referenced by some labeled formulation
- a label with no matching entry is checked inline as usual
- `because:` and `by:` are justification the checker only reference-validates;
  it never proves them

The same `have:`/`asserting:` group is also a clause (see Have / Asserting) and
a valid `declares:` item, where its label heading is optional. `Justification:`
replaces the older `Justified:` section and its `label:`/`by:` prose items."
Id: "4b6528c8-b596-45ae-87b5-74ce3419a2f6"
